# Build context hygiene.
#
# READ THIS FIRST, because the name is misleading. A SCORED image does NOT use
# this file. The board and the organizers' checker build each track with the
# TRACK FOLDER as the context:
#
#     docker build --network=none -t speeddemon/$TEAM-$TRACK:$COMMIT track-$TRACK
#
# so the ignore file that would apply to a scored build is
# `track-$TRACK/.dockerignore`, and there deliberately is none: a track folder
# holds only Dockerfile, build.sh, src/, README.md, PERF.md,
# .speed-demon.toml and verification/expected/, and every one of those belongs
# in the image. The Dockerfile's `COPY . /src` is intentional -- the spec makes
# the folder the whole build context.
#
# This root file therefore has one job: make a local `docker build .` from the
# repository root safe and unsurprising, so the two build paths cannot
# disagree about what the submission is. If you ever build from the root, this
# is what keeps the campaign's own tooling, documentation and datasets out of
# the image.

# Version control.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Host build output. Never ship the developer's copy: it is a binary of
# unknown provenance, and shipping it would hide a broken in-image build.
target/
bin/
track-*/run
track-*/run.exe
track-*/run.pdb

# The campaign's own infrastructure. Tooling, documentation and reference
# material are explicitly outside the four track folders, so they are never
# scored and must never enter an image.
tooling/
docs/
prep/
reference/
verification/
Makefile
check.py
*.bak

# Verification scratch and generated fixtures: reproducible from the public
# generators, and large.
verification/data/
verification/data-full/
verification/data-fixtures/
verification/data2/
verification/tmp/
verification/tmp2/

# Profiles and logs.
*.profdata
*.profraw
*.log

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
